Given three tables:

Students
Subjects
Examinations

The task was to find the number of times each student attended each subject exam, including cases where a student never attended a particular exam (count = 0).

Solution:- 

select st.student_id, st.student_name, su.subject_name, count(e.student_id) as attended_exams
from Students st
cross join Subjects su 
left join Examinations e
on st.student_id = e.student_id
and su.subject_name = e.subject_name
group by st.student_id, st.student_name, su.subject_name
order by st.student_id, st.student_name;
